    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for August 29th is anchored by two elite plays facing a soft matchup against R. Johnson. **Bryce Harper** (78.57) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53) are the clear cornerstones of the lineup, both benefiting from the 5.16 xERA of the opposing starter. **Harper** remains our highest-projected asset, with his xwOBA profile and high-leverage spot in the three-hole providing a high floor for HR and RBI production. **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) also warrants attention as a premium start; while facing Baz, **Butler** captures the benefits of a favorable park adjustment and a platoon edge that pushes his efficiency score well into the top tier. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (72.47) rounds out our core, leveraging a favorable platoon match against L. Lynch IV to maintain his consistent production across all five categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins came down to **Justin Crawford** (63.67) and **Jonathan Aranda** (63.10) versus our bench options. **Crawford** is a priority start today due to the extreme premium we place on SB potential, and despite an suboptimal spot in the nine-hole, his sprint-speed value outweighs the safer floor of **Jung Hoo Lee** (54.79). **Lee** was the strongest consideration for a bench spot but fell short; his lower dynamic platoon adjustment against L. Bratt made him the odd man out in a crowded OF rotation. We are closely monitoring the environment for **Gleyber Torres**, who carries a lower score (55.46) primarily due to a difficult matchup against B. Snell; the -15% SP Skill penalty serves as a firm reminder that despite his top-of-the-order usage, he is carrying significant risk today. **Cal Raleigh**, **Zack Gelof**, **Braden Montgomery**, and **Dylan Beavers** occupy the remainder of our active slots, all holding scores in the high 50s, which keeps them safely above our replacement-level threshold for the day.",
